`--no-rhsm` should be only needed when you have "subscription-manager"
installed on your systems, but why would you on a CentOS machine? :)

I'd rather suggest people should not have that installed.

As for CentOS Stream 8 being moved to vault, this is rather unrelated to the upgrade,
and I think people need to touch that on their systems anyway if they keep them alive after the EOL date.


What I did last week when I needed this was:

    sed -i 's/^mirrorlist/#&/; s/^#baseurl/baseurl/; s/mirror.centos.org/vault.centos.org/' /etc/yum.repos.d/CentOS-Stream-*.repo

I'll leave that here as a comment, not in the main post tho.
